From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Subject: [PATCH] avoid mixed declaration and code in v4l2_loopback_mmap()

v4l2_loopback_mmap() declares "u32 index" in the middle of the default:
case, after an if block. Kernels before 5.18 build with -std=gnu89 and
-Wdeclaration-after-statement, so this warns there; on a kernel built with
CONFIG_CC_WERROR=y (e.g. the BlackBerry KEY2 (athena) 4.19 tree) the build
fails:

  v4l2loopback.c:2294:17: error: ISO C90 forbids mixed declarations and
  code [-Werror=declaration-after-statement]

The variable is used once, so index the buffer array directly instead.
offset is already bounds-checked against image_size just above, so the
behaviour does not change.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 v4l2loopback.c | 3 +--
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/v4l2loopback.c b/v4l2loopback.c
index af9ec3e..224af45 100644
--- a/v4l2loopback.c
+++ b/v4l2loopback.c
@@ -2272,8 +2272,7 @@ static int v4l2_loopback_mmap(struct file *file, struct vm_area_struct *vma)
 			result = -EINVAL;
 			goto exit_mmap_unlock;
 		}
-		u32 index = offset / dev->buffer_size;
-		buffer = &dev->buffers[index];
+		buffer = &dev->buffers[offset / dev->buffer_size];
 		addr = dev->image + offset;
 		break;
 	}
